    "summary": "Cloth: a single strip of hand-spun and hand-woven cotton and silk. The ground weave is of white cotton in both warp and weft. Over this have been added pattern blocks of supplementary weft in dark indigo cotton and magenta alaari silk. The indigo and magenta blocks alternate along the strip, and form patterns of a lattice and rolling waves. The warp ends are cut but not hemmed.",
